result type guidance documentation is identified by "http://data.europa.eu/leg/lomo/lfds-CSA2#ResultType_GuidanceDocumentation".

result type guidance documentation has the type "owl:NamedIndividual".

result type guidance documentation is an action result type.

result type guidance documentation has the label "Guidance and Documentation".

result type guidance documentation has the explanation "Technical guidance, best practices, guidelines, methodologies, and advisory documents issued to support implementation of cybersecurity policies, practices, and Union legislation. Includes technical guidance, best practices, guidelines, incident response playbooks, methodologies for vulnerability disclosure, and advisory materials.".


result type reports analyses is identified by "http://data.europa.eu/leg/lomo/lfds-CSA2#ResultType_ReportsAnalyses".

result type reports analyses has the type "owl:NamedIndividual".

result type reports analyses is an action result type.

result type reports analyses has the label "Reports and Analyses".

result type reports analyses has the explanation "Formal reports, analyses, and assessments including annual reports, threat analyses, risk assessments, market analyses, technical situation reports, evaluation reports, and peer review reports. Covers all types of analytical outputs: annual activity reports, cyber threat analyses, coordinated risk assessments, market trend analyses, evaluation reports on certification schemes, peer review summaries, and technical assessments.".


result type advice opinions is identified by "http://data.europa.eu/leg/lomo/lfds-CSA2#ResultType_AdviceOpinions".

result type advice opinions has the type "owl:NamedIndividual".

result type advice opinions is an action result type.

result type advice opinions has the label "Advice and Opinions".

result type advice opinions has the explanation "Technical advice, expert opinions, recommendations, and assessments provided to support decision-making on cybersecurity matters, policy implementation, and compliance issues. Includes technical advice on implementation, expert opinions from ECCG or Advisory Group, recommendations on standards alignment or lessons learned implementation, and specific assessments of incidents, threats, or suppliers.".


result type alerts notifications is identified by "http://data.europa.eu/leg/lomo/lfds-CSA2#ResultType_AlertsNotifications".

result type alerts notifications has the type "owl:NamedIndividual".

result type alerts notifications is an action result type.

result type alerts notifications has the label "Alerts and Notifications".

result type alerts notifications has the explanation "Early alerts, warnings, and formal notifications regarding cybersecurity threats, incidents, changes, decisions, or compliance matters communicated to authorities, entities, or stakeholders. Encompasses early warnings on cyber threats, incident notifications, notifications of decisions or authorisations, communications on changes to implementation, and public communications on incidents.".


result type digital solutions databases is identified by "http://data.europa.eu/leg/lomo/lfds-CSA2#ResultType_DigitalSolutionsDatabases".

result type digital solutions databases has the type "owl:NamedIndividual".

result type digital solutions databases is an action result type.

result type digital solutions databases has the label "Digital Solutions, Databases and Repositories".

result type digital solutions databases has the explanation "Operational technical platforms, tools, digital solutions, databases, repositories, registries, and lists established, operated, maintained, and updated for cybersecurity purposes at Union level. Includes single reporting platforms for incident reporting, testing tools for conformity assessment, secure communications tools for CSIRTs network and EU-CyCLONe, cybersecurity maturity assessment tools, European Vulnerability Database, threat intelligence repositories, lessons learned repositories from exercises, registries of essential and important entities, lists of high-risk suppliers, public registers of Commission decisions, and repositories of certified products or services.".


result type frameworks schemes chemes is identified by "http://data.europa.eu/leg/lomo/lfds-CSA2#ResultType_FrameworksSchemesChemes".

result type frameworks schemes chemes has the type "owl:NamedIndividual".

result type frameworks schemes chemes is an action result type.

result type frameworks schemes chemes has the label "Frameworks, Schemes and Certificates".

result type frameworks schemes chemes has the explanation "European cybersecurity certification schemes, skills frameworks, attestation schemes, certificates, statements of conformity, and related technical specifications developed or issued under Union cybersecurity legislation. Includes European Cybersecurity Certification Schemes for ICT products/services/processes, European Cybersecurity Skills Framework (ECSF), individual skills attestation schemes, European cybersecurity certificates, EU statements of conformity, individual cybersecurity skills attestations, technical specifications, and model provisions for schemes.".


result type planning regulatory documents is identified by "http://data.europa.eu/leg/lomo/lfds-CSA2#ResultType_PlanningRegulatoryDocuments".

result type planning regulatory documents has the type "owl:NamedIndividual".

result type planning regulatory documents is an action result type.

result type planning regulatory documents has the label "Planning and Regulatory Documents".

result type planning regulatory documents has the explanation "Programming documents, work programmes, budget plans, implementing acts, delegated acts, decisions, rules of procedure, and other formal regulatory or planning instruments. Encompasses single programming documents, annual work programmes, rolling programmes of exercises, draft budget estimates, financial accounts, implementing acts defining key ICT assets or restrictions, delegated acts, formal decisions on authorisations or designations, rules of procedure for bodies, security rules for information handling, fee structures, and templates for standardised processes.".


requirement art 1 scope is identified by "http://data.europa.eu/leg/lomo/lfds-CSA2#Requirement_Art1_Scope".

requirement art 1 scope has the type "owl:NamedIndividual".

requirement art 1 scope is a constitutive rule.

requirement art 1 scope has the label "Article 1 - Subject Matter and Scope".

requirement art 1 scope is established in "https://data.europa.eu/eli/reg/2019/881/oj/eng/art_1".

requirement art 1 scope has the legal text "This Regulation lays down: (a) the mission, objectives, tasks and organisational matters relating to the European Union Agency for Cybersecurity (ENISA); (b) a framework for establishing European cybersecurity certification schemes for the purpose of ensuring an adequate level of cybersecurity for ICT products, ICT services, ICT processes, managed security services or the cybersecurity posture of entities in the Union, as well as for the purpose of avoiding the fragmentation of the internal market with regard to cybersecurity certification schemes in the Union; and (c) a trusted ICT supply chain framework. The framework referred to in paragraph 1, point (b) applies without prejudice to specific provisions in other Union legal acts regarding voluntary or mandatory certification. The framework referred to in the first subparagraph point (c) shall apply to public or private entities of a type referred to in Annex I or II to Directive (EU) 2022/2555 which provide their services or carry out their activities within the Union. This Regulation is without prejudice to the Member States' essential State functions, including ensuring the territorial integrity of the State, maintaining law and order and safeguarding national security. In particular, national security remains the sole responsibility of each Member State.".

requirement art 1 scope has the comment "Constitutive rule establishing the scope of the Regulation - defines three main frameworks (ENISA governance, cybersecurity certification, and trusted ICT supply chain), their application conditions, and safeguards for national security.".


